[size=5][b][color=#E8C88A]Wilder Wildlife - Customize Enemy Spawns[/color][/b][/size]
<br />
<br />Adjust boar herds and wolf packs from [b]10% to 200%[/b], with a separate switch for each species. [b]100% is the normal population and the default[/b]; 200% doubles the original population.
<br />
<br />Only ordinary wild boars and wolves are affected. Quest-gated, named and scripted encounters keep their normal values. Population scaling retains at least one animal; No spawn can leave an eligible group empty for one cycle.
<br />
<br />Optional replacements: Set independent boar and wolf replacement chances from 0% to 100%. Choose Bandits, Blood guards, Regular guards, Vidmo, Kobolds or No spawn for each species. Enabled choices have equal chances; an empty pool keeps the animals. A group keeps its choice through travel and save loading until its natural respawn. Replacement chances default to 0%.
<br />
<br />[size=4][b][color=#E8C88A]Configuration[/color][/b][/size]
<br />
<br />Open [b]Mod Settings &gt; Less Wildlife[/b], choose your settings and press Apply. Population changes take effect on later area encounters.
<br />
<br />[list]
<br />[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Base wildlife group size:[/color][/b] 10% to 200% in 1% steps. Applies to groups that remain wildlife; default 100%. Replacement enemies use their own size ranges. Quantities are rounded to the nearest animal.[/*]
<br />[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Adjust boars:[/color][/b] On applies the selected percentage to ordinary boar herds. Off restores original values still controlled by this mod. Default: On.[/*]
<br />[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Adjust wolves:[/color][/b] The same independent choice for ordinary wolf packs. Default: On.[/*]
<br />[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Logging:[/color][/b] Choose Off, Error, Warning, Info or Debug. Warning is the default; Off is silent. Debug records detailed troubleshooting information in Dawnwalker/Binaries/Win64/ue4ss/UE4SS.log.[/*]
<br />[/list]
<br />[color=#E6B980]Off disables population scaling for that species; it does not remove the animals.[/color] Already spawned animals are unaffected. Setting Base wildlife group size to 100% also restores original values still controlled by this mod. Changes made by the game or another mod are preserved.
<br />
<br />[size=3][b][color=#A8D5C2]Enemy group sizes[/color][/b][/size]
<br />Set minimum and maximum members separately for Bandits, Regular guards, Blood guards, Vidmo and Kobolds. Both limits accept [b]1–10[/b] and are shared by boar and wolf replacements. Every count in the inclusive range has equal chance. Equal limits give a fixed count; [b]1–1[/b] gives one enemy. Reversed limits are swapped.
<br />Defaults: Bandits [b]3–6[/b], Regular guards [b]2–4[/b], Blood guards [b]2–4[/b], Vidmo [b]1–2[/b], Kobolds [b]4–10[/b]. These counts override Base wildlife group size. No spawn remains a separate outcome.
<br />The enemy type and count stay with the group through travel, save loading and partial kills. Changes apply to new groups and later natural respawns; groups saved by an earlier version keep their current cycle's sizing. Encounter locations and respawn timing remain controlled by the game.
<br />
<br />[size=3][b][color=#A8D5C2]Manual configuration[/color][/b][/size]
<br />
<br />Launch the game once to create settings.ini, then close it. Open this file inside your The Blood of Dawnwalker game folder:
<br />
<br />[code]Dawnwalker&#92;Binaries&#92;Win64&#92;ue4ss&#92;Mods&#92;LessWildlife&#92;settings.ini[/code]
<br />[code][LessWildlife]
<br />populationPercent = 100
<br />reduceBoars = 1
<br />reduceWolves = 1
<br />logLevel = 2[/code]
<br />Use an integer from 10 to 200 for populationPercent. For the species switches, use 0 for Off or 1 for On. logLevel uses 0–4 for Off, Error, Warning, Info and Debug. Keep the generated replacement keys; the included README lists them. Save and restart the game.
<br />
<br />Unusually large areas or very dense bursts of encounters keep their current population values until a later encounter can be handled.
<br />
<br />[size=4][b][color=#E8C88A]Installation[/color][/b][/size]
<br />
<br />[list]
<br />[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Vortex:[/color][/b] Install Less-Wildlife.zip through Vortex, enable it and deploy.[/*]
<br />[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Manual:[/color][/b] Copy the archive's Data/LessWildlife folder into &lt;The Blood of Dawnwalker&gt;/Dawnwalker/Binaries/Win64/ue4ss/Mods, preserving the folder structure.[/*]
<br />[/list]
<br />[size=4][b][color=#E8C88A]Reporting Bugs and other issues[/color][/b][/size]
<br />
<br />If you encounter an issue, set [b]Logging[/b] to [b]Debug[/b] in this mod’s Mod Setting Menu settings, apply the change, reproduce the issue. Then start either a bug report in the Bugs tab on Nexus (preferred method for me to track things), or at least start a new thread in comments and send me [b]Dawnwalker/Binaries/Win64/ue4ss/UE4SS.log[/b] from your game folder. Do not report unrelated bugs in other people's threads, please, this makes it impossible for me to track issues.
<br />
<br />
<br />
